# Dev only. Vite gives .env.development priority over .env, so `npm run dev`
# talks to the proxy defined in vite.config.js instead of calling the API
# directly. That keeps requests same-origin, which is what lets the app work
# from a Codespace or tunnel hostname -- the API's CORS allowlist only covers
# http://localhost:5173 and :5174, so a direct call from any other hostname is
# blocked by the browser.
#
# Production builds are unaffected: they still read the absolute URL from .env.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
